# Claude Code Dev Container — Environment Configuration
# -------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is in .gitignore — never commit it.
# .env.example IS committed — it documents what's needed.


# =============================================================================
# HOW VALUES ARE RESOLVED
# =============================================================================
# A value written as $SOMETHING is a reference, not a literal. mosh looks it up
# in your host shell environment (~/.zshenv) at launch and passes the resolved
# value into the container. Only variables named in this file are forwarded —
# your full host environment is never leaked.
#
# Keeping the real values in ~/.zshenv means host-native Claude Code (run
# outside any container) and containerized Claude Code share one configuration.


# =============================================================================
# Authentication — choose ONE (or none for OAuth)
# =============================================================================

# --- Option A: OAuth (Claude Pro/Max) ---
# Leave the keys below commented out. Claude Code will prompt you to
# log in via browser on first launch. Tokens persist in config/.

# --- Option B: LiteLLM gateway (NIST) ---
# Put the real values in ~/.zshenv, then uncomment these references:
#
#   export NIST_LITELLM_KEY="sk-..."
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="$NIST_LITELLM_KEY"
#   export ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="https://your-gateway.example.gov"
#
# The key is referenced as $NIST_LITELLM_KEY rather than $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# because mosh unsets ANTHROPIC_API_KEY before reading this file, so that host
# credentials don't bleed into projects that didn't ask for them.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=$NIST_LITELLM_KEY
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=$ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX=0

# --- Option C: Direct Anthropic API key ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Option D: Google Cloud / Vertex AI ---
# ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id
# CLOUD_ML_REGION=us-east5


# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: Path overrides
# =============================================================================

# Path to your gcloud config directory on the host (Vertex AI only).
# Only change this if your gcloud config lives somewhere non-standard.
# GCLOUD_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gcloud

# Path where Claude Code's config is persisted on the host.
# This keeps your MCP settings, Claude config, and history across runs.
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-dev-config


# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: MCP server credentials
# =============================================================================

# OpenBrain personal MCP server (https://github.com/mfaughn/openbrain)
# If set, the open-brain MCP server will be available inside every container.
# Get your key from the openbrain project's vars file.
# OPENBRAIN_MCP_KEY=your-key-here


# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: GitHub authentication
# =============================================================================

# Personal access token for git push/pull inside the container.
# When set, mosh configures git to authenticate over HTTPS using this token
# and transparently rewrites SSH remote URLs to HTTPS (inside the container
# only — your host repo remotes are never modified).
# GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=ghp_...


# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: Claude Code model selection
# =============================================================================

# Tier aliases. These define what the words "opus", "sonnet" and "haiku"
# resolve to, which is what /model opus, /fast, opusplan and subagent model
# selection all rely on. Required when using a gateway that renames models.
# ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=$ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL
# ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=$ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL
# ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=$ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL

# Pin one specific model as the main model. Leave this unset when using the
# tier aliases above — a pin overrides them, and a stale value here is a
# common cause of "why am I still on the old model?".
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
